Includes routers, switches, servers, and end devices working together.  
Networks are classified as LAN, WAN, or MAN based on coverage.

---

### 📶 Wireless and Mobile Networks
Uses radio waves (Wi-Fi, cellular) to connect devices without cables.  
Offers mobility but may face interference and signal limitations.

---

### 🏠 Building a Home Network
Involves connecting devices through a router using wired or wireless methods.  
Provides internet access, file sharing, and smart device connectivity.

---

### 🔁 Communication Principles
Data transmission follows protocols, encoding, and addressing rules.  
Ensures reliable and accurate delivery between sender and receiver.

---

### 🔌 Network Media
Includes copper cables, fiber optics, and wireless transmission.  
Each medium differs in speed, cost, and transmission distance.

---

### 🧩 Access Layer
The layer where end devices connect to the network.  
Handles network access, security, and data entry.

